\title{A metadata node: \code{\verb~|a = mdata b~} is another term for the official caches}
\taxon{Example}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{soundness}
\tag{loader}
\tag{reference-engine}
\meta{origin}{docs/design/review/reference-caches.md}
\meta{updated}{2026-11-24}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The loader drops metadata records, so the reference engine saw \code{\verb~|a = b~} where the export says \code{\verb~|a = mdata b~}. Officially the node is a term of its own. Source: [the audit of the reference engine's caches](rep-reference-caches), sections 0 and 1, and finding S3-F2 of [the adversarial review of the default set](rep-soundness-default-set); [the exactness session](ses-874D).}
\pre{\verb~|
-- a, b, use as in the box example;  b' = mdata b
-- one theorem:  And.intro W (And.intro W0 W2)
--   W  = use (a = b)  (Eq.refl a)     true while the cache is empty
--   W0 = use (a = 5)  (Eq.refl 5)     the full reduction of a is cached: 5
--   W2 = use (a = b') (Eq.refl a)

s3-wc-pos-mdata-bad        official: REJECT    reference engine: accept
s3-mdata-eager-hidden-ok   official: accept    reference engine: reject
~}
\ul{
\li{If \code{\verb~|b'~} is the same term as \code{\verb~|b~} for the caches, the set of successful pairs answers \code{\verb~|W2~} and the theorem is accepted. Officially \code{\verb~|mdata b~} is a different key, the cheap reduction of \code{\verb~|a~} now answers \code{\verb~|5~}, and \code{\verb~|W2~} fails.}
\li{The second export goes the other way: officially a metadata node hides an application of \code{\verb~|eagerReduce~} from the syntactic test, the comparison is plain and true. An engine that sees through the node compares in eager mode and rejects.}
\li{The statement accepted in the first export is derivable, so the divergence is of the tolerated kind. Under the practical policy metadata stays transparent; the strict mode declines a declaration whose type or value carries a metadata node.}
\li{The rejection of the second export is not tolerated, and it is gone since the evening of 2026-11-24: the loader declines a declaration with a node around an application of \code{\verb~|eagerReduce~} under both policies, see [the changelog entry](log-6K9N). A second way in which a dropped node makes the engines reject an official accept is [the example of the beta redex](ex-FD6K).}
}
\p{Used by [metadata nodes and the nondep flag are part of the official term identity](ins-61D4).}
\p{See also: [the caches of the reference engine](design-reference-caches).}
